\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the Active GLiNER framework. Data is first evaluated in zero-shot mode, then training examples are ranked by uncertainty using active learning strategies (LC, MNLP, MSE). The top-ranked examples are used for LoRA fine-tuning (Fit) with ground truth, LLM, or mixed labels. The fine-tuned model produces predictions (Predict) which are evaluated on the test set. The feedback loop from Predict back to Ranking enables iterative refinement.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{3}{Overview of the Active GLiNER framework. Data is first evaluated in zero-shot mode, then training examples are ranked by uncertainty using active learning strategies (LC, MNLP, MSE). The top-ranked examples are used for LoRA fine-tuning (Fit) with ground truth, LLM, or mixed labels. The fine-tuned model produces predictions (Predict) which are evaluated on the test set. The feedback loop from Predict back to Ranking enables iterative refinement}{figure.caption.1}{}}
