\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Threshold analysis on MIT Movies test set. GLiNER Base and Fine-Tuned (FT) models are evaluated at confidence thresholds 0.1, 0.5, and 0.9, compared against the LLM baseline (Gemma 3 12B). Fine-tuned GLiNER at threshold 0.5 achieves the best balance of precision and recall, outperforming the LLM on F\textsubscript  {1}{}.}}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:threshold}{{2}{4}{Threshold analysis on MIT Movies test set. GLiNER Base and Fine-Tuned (FT) models are evaluated at confidence thresholds 0.1, 0.5, and 0.9, compared against the LLM baseline (Gemma 3 12B). Fine-tuned GLiNER at threshold 0.5 achieves the best balance of precision and recall, outperforming the LLM on \fone {}}{figure.caption.3}{}}
